# id: M47-superseded-split-applied-anyway
# covering-test: TestASupersededSplitIsRefused
# package: ./store/
# expect: killed
# power-unreachable: census identity, 300 seeds, 76 fields -- the sweep cannot produce this schedule. Raft's figure-8 rule serialises it: a new leader must commit an entry of its own before it can commit the previous term's split, and committing it means applying it, which moves the extent before a second split can be proposed from it. Zero firings in 300 A4 seeds, recorded in DESIGN-A4 section 10 as an unexercised path rather than as evidence. The guard is induced directly instead, which is what a floor could not have told us. RE-MEASURED under current at A6's close with the repaired probe, and UPGRADED: 0 of 300 per-seed, sweepfail=0, and the accumulated census is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the unmutated tree's across all four shards -- 0 of 76 fields move. That is a stronger claim than the old 'zero firings', which was a detection claim and therefore compatible with the defect happening unnoticed, as M62 turned out to be. Same disposition and same instrument as M66 and M30: UNREACHED and proved (DESIGN-A6 section 42). NO OTHER DETECTOR: census identity is the strongest instrument this harness has -- if no field the harness counts moves, there is nothing for any detector to see, and a rate or a sweep verdict is a strictly weaker view of the same run. Re-asked by the refutation pass at 30 seeds and still byte-identical, which re-asks the claim rather than restating it
# power-refute-claim: census-identical
